# TestOps Metadata Sync

When updating Playwright autotests, keep metadata aligned with TestOps.

- Test name format: `<Readable test name> @allure.id:<number>`.
- `@allure.id` must be at the end of the test name.
- Keep only one `@allure.id` marker per test.
- If TestOps ID changes, update only the numeric part and keep readable title stable.
- If TestOps case does not exist yet, keep readable title without fake IDs.

Use Allure labels in each autotest:

- `allure.label("feature", "<Feature>")`
- `allure.label("story", "<Story>")`

Examples:

- Good: `test("Создание новой задачи @allure.id:19", async () => {})`
- Bad: `test("@allure.id:19 Создание новой задачи", async () => {})`
- Bad: `test("Создание новой задачи @allure.id:19 @allure.id:20", async () => {})`
